  "id": "COMPOUND:28035 - PROTEIN:5849",
  "verbalization": "Gramideoxybenzoin B is implicated in the targeting of SNU-387, a compound that is itself a target of multiple related molecules, including Quercetagetin 3-methyl ether 7-glucoside and 5-Hydroxy-6,8-Dimethoxy-2,3-Dimethylbenzo[G]Chromen-4-One. All three of these compounds share a common mechanism of action, targeting A549 cells, a human lung cancer cell line. The evidence suggests that Gramideoxybenzoin B may act through a shared pathway, possibly by modulating the same molecular targets or influencing similar cellular processes in A549 cells. The high scores in the visible paths indicate a strong, consistent relationship between Gramideoxybenzoin B and A549, likely due to the shared target profile and the involvement of SNU-387, which is a known target of multiple compounds with potential anti-cancer activity. The integration of these findings supports the hypothesis that Gramideoxybenzoin B may exert its effects on A549 cells through a mechanism involving the modulation of a common set of molecular targets, potentially through a shared biological pathway or function.",
